{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts","id":622655,"title":"[Ex3] Sidereals, Charms and Character Concepts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-10T14:38:23-07:00","id":622655,"title":"[Ex3] Sidereals, Charms and Character Concepts","content":"So... I'm kind of drunk <i>and</i> procrastinating right now, so I thought I'd write about some Sidereal charms I don't like, why I don't like them and what I'd like to see in Third Edition. Nothing specific, more like some trends that seem problematic and what approach could make things easier for me as a player. <br /> <br /> Like the fact that Sidereals have about a dozen charms to summon spirits. Now, I've got a problem with Spirit-Binding Battle Pattern because it's fueled by human sacrifice and any spirit you summon using it will suck unless you have four other Sidereals working with you, but the bigger problem there is that spirits are complete shit, which going by Ahlat's charms in Third Edition, is no longer a problem. That still leaves a couple of Charms like Water and Fire Legion, Sky Spirit Demand and one of the effects of Terminal Sanction, not to mention sorcery and thaumaturgy. Plus, you know, I'm a goddamn Sidereal. I don't need charms or magic to bind spirits to my service when I can just walk up to them and politely ask for a favour. <br /> <br /> Which brings me to my next point. I'm going to assume that Sidereals had all these charms in second edition because social combat as a system was completely fucked, so binding spirits was the only real option for Sidereal social charms. I would absolutely love it if Sidereals had social influence charms like Mark of Exaltation that made it easier for them to interact with spirits through social influence. If I'm going to play a respected member of the Celestial Bureaucracy, I expect to have powers that allow me to act like a respected member of the Celestial Bureaucracy. I don't want to have to magically enslave the people I'm supposed to work with on a daily basis. <br /> <br /> And another thing. I'm iffy on the fact that Sidereals get their familiar charms in Ride instead of Survival like Solars do, but I'm mostly okay with it. If I'm going to get a divine familiar, I might as well ride it anyway. I really wish Sidereals charms were more applicable to the ability they were slotted under so Sidereals aren't complete shit at riding animals, but that's another problem. No, my problem with Sidereal Ride is Riding the Dragon. <br /> <br /> Let's say I've got this crane familiar. I raised it as my familiar. I used Spirit-Shape Companion and Godly Companion to turn that crane into my most loyal companion. We traveled all over Creation and kicked ass together. Maybe I even thought it some of my kung fu just because I could. I have invested a hell of a lot of time and experience into that crane. And then I use Riding the Dragon to turn that crane into a fucking dragon so we can kill Octavian together or something and once the charm ends, that crane is gone forever. That's bullshit. Don't get me wrong, I would love to play a Sidereal who goes around finding animals with auspicious destinies, claiming them as familiars, uplifting them into divinity and then ultimately releasing them as elemental dragons, but it's not something I would ever do with a familiar I actually want to keep around. The whole thing just seems like a complete waste, like the charm tree <i>doesn't</i> want me to play a Sidereal with a familiar. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T14:56:53-07:00","id":622693,"title":"","content":"Fuck Riding the Dragon <i>so hard</i>.<br /> <br /> The problem with Riding the Dragon is that it's not a fuck-up. The way it works fully makes sense within the overall design of Sidereals. It does exactly what it's supposed to do.<br /> <br /> And that... that reveals intrinsic, underlying motifs to Sidereals that are bothersome. Because the original design behind them is excellent, most of this is obfuscated, or sold to the reader much more skillfully in such a fashion that people don't realize the darkness.<br /> <br /> But Riding the Dragon is an in your face reminder. Riding the Dragon is that Charm which is there as a statement that the underlying motif of being a Sidereal is of being the kind of person who nurtures relationships with mortals, or animal familiars, over years or decades, and then when it's convenient for you you just coldly lobotomize them for a temporary boost in power.<br /> <br /> Riding the Dragon flatly rubs your face in the fact that <i>Sidereals are assholes</i> working for an <i>asshole bureaucracy of assholes</i> whose job involves<i> being an asshole for the &quot;greater good&quot;</i> except the greater good is <i>coordinated by corrupt assholes who want bribes</i>. And this is intentional! This is the original perfect Moran design, not a screw-up! Exalted: the Sidereals is that book where a young Seer grabs a mortal she's known for years and lobotomizes him because she needs to arrive somewhere faster than her Gold Faction rivals.<br /> <br /> If you look closely, the entire design of Sidereals is underlain with such dark, cynical motifs which grin wickedly at you from between the lines. And that's... that's often ignored because ignoring it is easier. And honestly? I'm fine with ignoring it. I'm not sure I want to play the kind of person who uses Riding the Dragon or Shun the Smiling Lady or any battle-pattern which work better if you consciously attempt to maximize casualties for your own side to fuel it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T14:58:16-07:00","id":622696,"title":"","content":"Sidereal charms are the strongest proof that the Maidens hate their own chosen.<br /> <br /> I'll post more on this when I am not working late.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T15:19:14-07:00","id":622711,"title":"","content":"I do not foresee good things for this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T15:19:40-07:00","id":622712,"title":"","content":"Ride the Dragon is a pretty cool Charm, particularly since you can just place the Bridle of Mercury on whichever fool you want dragon'd. Sacrificing actual friends and allies is for truly desperate straits.<br /> <br /> The duration <i>could</i> stand to be longer. Spending five actions to lobotomize someone for a scenelong is just <i>wasteful</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T15:21:29-07:00","id":622714,"title":"","content":"In theory I like that the Sidereals have different Charms for dealing with different sorts of spirits that grow from different places, although I would prefer that they were not &quot;forceful&quot; by default.<br /> <br /> I do have to agree that, even if I do think it's overstating to say like Omicron does that Sidereal Ride makes that statement, I really am probably not so keen on reflection that selecting Favoured and Caste Abilities locks characters in to cascades which have a set degree of coercion and exploitation (Ride is coercive and exploitative, to a lesser extent so are Socialise and Presence, Performance and Linguistics aren't). It's very attractive that each tree has a story and theme expressed in a sutra, but...<br /> <br /> I hope they would find a different strategy that changes the feel of these, so that each tree is clearly distinct in theme without locking a character into using exploitative magic just because a particular Ability is his style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T15:28:50-07:00","id":622721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=622693#post622693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Riding the Dragon flatly rubs your face in the fact that <i>Sidereals are assholes</i> working for an <i>asshole bureaucracy of assholes</i> whose job involves<i> being an asshole for the &quot;greater good&quot;</i> except the greater good is <i>coordinated by corrupt assholes who want bribes</i>. And this is intentional! This is the original perfect Moran design, not a screw-up! Exalted: the Sidereals is that book where a young Seer grabs a mortal she's known for years and lobotomizes him because she needs to arrive somewhere faster than her Gold Faction rivals.<br /> <br /> If you look closely, the entire design of Sidereals is underlain with such dark, cynical motifs which grin wickedly at you from between the lines. And that's... that's often ignored because ignoring it is easier. And honestly? I'm fine with ignoring it. I'm not sure I want to play the kind of person who uses Riding the Dragon or Shun the Smiling Lady or any battle-pattern which work better if you consciously attempt to maximize casualties for your own side to fuel it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't mind that Sidereals are assholes if it wasn't for the fact that they're assholes to the people they are supposed to get along with in order to do their jobs. Hell, Sidereal charms that exclusively fuck over other Exalted might work well with the way the Bronze and Gold factions are set up. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=622711#post622711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not foresee good things for this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>So long as those not good things happen before I sober up. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T15:31:03-07:00","id":622724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=622721#post622721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So long as those not good things happen before I sober up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am right there with you.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T17:04:44-07:00","id":622837,"title":"","content":"My problem with Riding the Dragon is that it kind of fails at its intended purpose.<br /> The Heavenly Gates and Stormwind Rider can generally get a group of Sidereals to wherever they need to go fast enough and I can get behind this charm as providing emergency speed except its very rare that 100 miles per hour is too slow yet 500 miles per hour is sufficient and for fate of the world type stuff it is also competing with the Greater Sign of Mercury.<br /> <br /> Thus its common to play up how <i>awesome</i> being a dragon is going to be for a mortal and have exploits involving creating armies of the things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T00:05:31-07:00","id":623971,"title":"","content":"I had fun with Riding the Dragon. Even used it on my favorite godly familiar. I did pay the willpower to NOT lobotomize it and let it become a true elemental dragon.<br /> <br /> I then promoted it with that one Charm whose name I forgot and eventually even married him (with the Charm of course, that was so broken pre 2.5). I actually permanently turned several of my familiars into Dragons and put them into favorable positions in the Bureau of Seasons.<br /> <br /> I readily admit the ST was not too difficult on letting me recoup on some of the xp cost by granting allies, contacts, backing and such.<br /> <br /> But still, using it to create a mount or as muscle in a fight? Nah, it was pretty useless for that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T06:13:30-07:00","id":624181,"title":"","content":"It's really one of the Sidereals' big things, hard choices and difficult sacrifices. It shows up all over the place for them. Their charms reinforce it by regularly asking them to make a difficult choice. It helps to keep some balance in terms of fate.<br /> <br /> They sacrifice their personal lives for their job, they sacrificed the greatness of the First Age for the security of Creation, they sacrificed to ability to develop real relationships with people to avoid getting arrested and executed for their crimes. <br /> <br /> Now it can be argued that some of the charms aren't good enough for the sacrifice, buy it isn't out of theme to sacrifice an army to win a war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T06:32:29-07:00","id":624195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=622837#post622837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Heavenly Gates and Stormwind Rider can generally get a group of Sidereals to wherever they need to go fast enough and I can get behind this charm as providing emergency speed except </span></span></span>its very rare that 100 miles per hour is too slow yet 500 miles per hour is sufficient</div> </div> </div> </div>It feels kind of weird to me to assess speed in terms of needing to make things in time for an emergency.<br /> <br /> I think the one big difference, and the one that would be of concern to almost anybody who ever had need to consider it in real life, is that 500 mph means you get an extra four hours that would have otherwise been wasted.<br /> <br /> It's like asking why anybody took a plane to different parts of the United States when they've got perfectly good cars.<br /> <br /> Not even just about more time at whatever your destination is, just because of how <i>tedious</i> long travel is.<br /> <br /> That's on top of how you get to arrive at your destination with an engine of destruction.<br /> <br /> Still, all of that still strikes me as ancillary to the basic point of the pinnacle of the Heavenly Sage concept of riding being able to pull out a big riding dragon (and how it builds on the prior Heavenly Sage riding ideas of approaching relationships in terms of handling beasts of burden).<br /> <br /> Sometimes Charms should just be there in order to capture a character image rather than be measured optimally against all other options.<br /> <br /> Prince Diamond is probably riding around slower than a Stormwind Rider spell or a Sidereal dragon and all (although probably a fair bit faster than most mortal riders), and it doesn't matter because being a sorcerer is not really the point there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T06:47:25-07:00","id":624226,"title":"","content":"I feel that in 2e, especially, there was this feeling that sorcery is so useful that when you got to a certain level of essence, there was this assumption that a celestial would invest in it. And it was more a case of background justifying why not, rather than why. Sorcerery became a bit of a norm.<br /> <br /> I'd prefer it if Sorcery was once more treated as weird and esotoric, difficult to attain and mysterious in nature. I'd want most Celestials to not be sorcerers, I'd want the ones that are to be seen as somewhat apart, beholden to strange forces and hidden occult laws.<br /> <br /> That way, nobody would say &quot;who needs Riding the Dragon when you can summon a Demon Wasp?&quot; as the assumption would be that the majority of Sidereals can't summon a Demon Wasp, and aren't going to learn to either. Remember, Sorcery is harder to attain, in setting, than the mechanics allow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T07:01:24-07:00","id":624237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=624195#post624195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like asking why anybody took a plane to different parts of the United States when they've got perfectly good cars.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the plane required you to sacrifice another human being as a source of fuel then I like to think most people would be inclined to consider the car sufficient for their needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","user":"Bastet","date":". 08-12-2015, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T07:12:29-07:00","id":624251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=622696#post622696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereal charms are the strongest proof that the Maidens hate their own chosen.<br /> <br /> I'll post more on this when I am not working late.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that I am no longer in a bad mood because of work. I'll soften this by saying that the Sidereal Charm set is proof that the maidens are bitches. They may not hate their chosen, but they have a strange concept of &quot;Love&quot;. I imagine the Maidens' relationship with their Chosen much like Harry Dresden's Relationship with Mab in Cold Days. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=624237#post624237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the plane required you to sacrifice another human being as a source of fuel then I like to think most people would be inclined to consider the car sufficient for their needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am perfectly fine with the Sidereal theme of Sacrifice, but I would prefer that if I have to sacrifice my pet dog, it be for something more than a sweet ride.<br /> <br /> Now I have to think up some literary examples of heroes sacrificing something to accomplish a greater goal. So far, the only one I can think of is Azor Ahai and the Lightbringer from Game of Thrones. Also, Arya sacrificing her identity to become an Assassin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T07:13:26-07:00","id":624252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=624226#post624226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That way, nobody would say &quot;who needs Riding the Dragon when you can summon a Demon Wasp?&quot; as the assumption would be that the majority of Sidereals can't summon a Demon Wasp, and aren't going to learn to either. Remember, Sorcery is harder to attain, in setting, than the mechanics allow.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, that runs into conflict with other Sidereal themes, one of which is their closed Charmset.<br /> <br /> With a closed Charmset, damn near every Sidereal is going to be initiated into Sorcery and learn Martial Arts, because the Sidereal Charmset is optimized fully for them in their role as Viziers to the Solars and agents of the Bureau of Destiny, and it works great for those two things but is complete shit at anything else. Astrology is more flexible but is subtle rather than direct and also limited in scope. (Let's ignore for a bit the bad mechanics behind it.)<br /> <br /> Sidereals who want to expand their skillsets flexibly and powerfully have to learn Sorcery and/or Martial Arts. That's a major theme behind them and one of the bedrocks of their design, that Sidereals are sifus and sorcerers, unable to flexibly channel their essence in the way other Exalted can but masters of the martial arts and with their fingers on the strands of fate.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the Sidereals still have much of their infrastructure in place and unlike the Dragon-Blooded don't have a societal taboo against sorcery.<br /> <br /> With all those facts in place, it is usually safe to assume any Sidereal of any age at all has at least been initiated into sorcery and knows a few spells, if for no other reason than that Spell-Shattering Palm, while pretty great, is hard to learn and not nearly as flexible as Sapphire Countermagic, and the work they do means they're going to bump up against assholes wielding the Emerald Circle an awful lot.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T07:17:59-07:00","id":624256,"title":"","content":"The other odd thing about Riding the Dragon is that it was created before the Primordial War, and lesser elemental dragons didn't exist until a century or something after the War ended. It's like the weirdness of the anti-undead Medicine charms, except those revealed their purpose as soon as the first Neverborn died.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Sidereals were creating these creatures that didn't correspond to anything in real life, and apparently? didn't choose to (or know how, or have the ability to) make the transformations permanent until after lesser elemental dragons evolved naturally... It's somewhat strange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T07:21:24-07:00","id":624262,"title":"","content":"People like to focus on the whole &quot;sacrifice person&quot; thing because it's all punchy and scary and fits into this big narrative momentum of callous Sidereals that things like Shun the Smiling Lady all goes into.<br /> <br /> So they overlook the fact that it can also be used on animals, and that Sidereals have a Ride Charm to make any animal in a vicinity submit to being your Familiar.<br /> <br /> Second Edition made that Charm a bit less costly (it dropped the experience point cost, and for Breaking the Wild Mortal as well), which I'm a bit unsure about; on the one hand, it will be a bit more palatable to people who complain about anything indefinite having an XP cost, but on the other I feel it makes the option of just fixing the Bridle to any random animal or person in the vicinity a bit too easy, both increasing the viability of Riding the Dragon while reducing much sense of dilemma or consideration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the plane required you to sacrifice another human being as a source of fuel then I like to think most people would be inclined to consider the car sufficient for their needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals are not most people. Whether or not they have a Charm like Riding the Dragon doesn't matter; pretty much every Sidereal in Heaven is complicit in the suffering and death of pretty much everyone who suffers and dies, either when they need to personally arrange for it to happen or because they're standing in a position to see it happening and not intervene.<br /> <br /> This shouldn't equate to using a Charm like Riding the Dragon lightly or frequently, but it also means that a Sidereal who would adamantly refuse to use it at all is... not exactly weird, but they're adopting a position of significance to how the execute their general duties.<br /> <br /> Sidereals have a lot to do, and it might not behove them to select a slower path.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T07:56:08-07:00","id":624330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=624262#post624262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals have a lot to do, and it might not behove them to select a slower path.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you misunderstand my issue with Ride the Dragon as some kind of moral objection.<br /> <br /> My issues is that-<br /> Miles per hour speeds in a Storyteller game are almost completely arbitrary which hurts the idea of it being a necessary sacrifice.<br /> My experience is that the charm almost never gets used like it was in the chapter fiction of Exalted: the Sidereals, I have seen literally one instance of it used that way by an antagonist who was also a rapist.<br /> <br /> Its not that it should not exist, its that its failing very badly at what it was intended to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","user":"Bastet","date":". 08-12-2015, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T08:11:31-07:00","id":624369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=624262#post624262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People like to focus on the whole &quot;sacrifice person&quot; thing because it's all punchy and scary and fits into this big narrative momentum of callous Sidereals that things like Shun the Smiling Lady all goes into.<br /> <br /> So they overlook the fact that it can also be used on animals, and that Sidereals have a Ride Charm to make any animal in a vicinity submit to being your Familiar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm mostly okay with that, setting the XP cost aside. It's just that if I have a charm that turns my familiar into a dragon, I would like to use it on the familiar I've invested in the most... which I can't do without losing my familiar one way or the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T08:58:22-07:00","id":624406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=622712#post622712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The duration <i>could</i> stand to be longer. Spending five actions to lobotomize someone for a scenelong is just <i>wasteful</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was a 2nd edition mistake but it goes back to 1st edition too.<br /> I think the intention is that you travel off-screen but it would be amusing if having a scene of the PCs conversing among themselves or encountering something in the air caused the charm to end abruptly and as a result Sidereals with that charm having lots of pockets that are perpetually full of small rodents in case of unforseen circumstances in the air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T09:08:37-07:00","id":624423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=624251#post624251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I am no longer in a bad mood because of work. I'll soften this by saying that the Sidereal Charm set is proof that the maidens are bitches. They may not hate their chosen, but they have a strange concept of &quot;Love&quot;. I imagine the Maidens' relationship with their Chosen much like Harry Dresden's Relationship with Mab in Cold Days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feels a little reductive to me. The Maidens are incredibly devoted to events playing out in a particular way they foresee. In the Glories interpretation, this extends to an ability to see a vision of how things will proceed and then having simply no choice about whether they carry it out.<br /> <br /> There's a very real possibility that the Sidereals -- Charmset and all -- are what they are because the Maidens literally could not have made their Exaltations any other way if they'd tried. By itself, this would say little if anything about how they feel about it, nor how they might have preferred it to be had they free reign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Minor rephrasing and tweaking. 08-12-2015, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T10:46:30-07:00","id":624500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=624181#post624181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really one of the Sidereals' big things, hard choices and difficult sacrifices. It shows up all over the place for them. Their charms reinforce it by regularly asking them to make a difficult choice. It helps to keep some balance in terms of fate.<br /> <br /> They sacrifice their personal lives for their job, they sacrificed the greatness of the First Age for the security of Creation, they sacrificed to ability to develop real relationships with people to avoid getting arrested and executed for their crimes.<br /> <br /> Now it can be argued that some of the charms aren't good enough for the sacrifice, buy it isn't out of theme to sacrifice an army to win a war.</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider this in the context of Sidereal &quot;fishboning&quot;.<br /> <br /> It takes a lot more work to convince the audience that the Sidereal choking someone on a fishbone is a hero doing what is necessary, in terms of showing them the consequences if they don't and the reason why they must and there is no other option, than just skipping to &quot;Sidereal makes sure baby chokes on a fishbone, is hero, saved world. Fate says so, even if it never shows you why.&quot;.<br /> <br /> Same thing with Charms that work on sacrifice - you have to create a methodology where that sacrifice could have been avoidable by otherwise or the player otherwise chose that as an option, so they own it, rather than the player being forced into a bloody sacrifice by their magic, and sort of make it believable that the Charm requires that balance and that in that situation, the sacrifice is valid . <br /> <br /> Random magic that just happens to kill or hurt people doesn't really create the vibe of a hero making difficult sacrifices, so much as like &quot;These guys randomly have magic which is indifferent to human life and suffering, or is parasitic on people, and its questionable that they use it to improve any human people's welfare. Why and how are they heroes again?&quot;. If you have to sacrifice an army to win a war because, you know, it's the 300 or something, and they must defend that pass, even if they die, that's different than it just being because of magic.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying I got that vibe from JM's Sidereal Charms exactly, just it seems quite difficult to get that theme of sacrifice across through Charms alone, without the inadvertant implications. It might be better to not try and do that too much through Charms, rather than story.<br /> <br /> Obviously this is not me arguing for overly sanitised Charms, just that it might help to write Charms that are trying to convey sacrifice with these ideas in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T11:38:13-07:00","id":624524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=624252#post624252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, that runs into conflict with other Sidereal themes, one of which is their closed Charmset.<br /> <br /> With a closed Charmset, damn near every Sidereal is going to be initiated into Sorcery and learn Martial Arts, because the Sidereal Charmset is optimized fully for them in their role as Viziers to the Solars and agents of the Bureau of Destiny, and it works great for those two things but is complete shit at anything else. Astrology is more flexible but is subtle rather than direct and also limited in scope. (Let's ignore for a bit the bad mechanics behind it.)<br /> <br /> Sidereals who want to expand their skillsets flexibly and powerfully have to learn Sorcery and/or Martial Arts. That's a major theme behind them and one of the bedrocks of their design, that Sidereals are sifus and sorcerers, unable to flexibly channel their essence in the way other Exalted can but masters of the martial arts and with their fingers on the strands of fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although on a side topic to discussion between you and Solar, this is one of those things I kind of find interesting, as.... <br /> <br /> In a lot of the discussions we've had around 3e, there is this idea that Exalts are good at what they're good at, and not just capable of rewiring what they are good at because they have spare experience or want some capability. If you're a sorceror, then that's a trait only certain Exalts have, and that mindset to become a sorceror is in their nature, in a sense (this idea is roughly paraphrasing Solar's statement).<br /> <br /> And the incentives around the most Exalted align with this - there's always plenty more depth you can explore in any ability, without needing to branch off into other abilities that aren't within your character's, er... character or into evocations or sorcery or MA when it's inappropriate for the character.<br /> <br /> With Sidereals, not so much. It doesn't matter so much if you have a concept that a character is just not good at an Ability, there is are incentives towards buying into other Abilities or into sorcery or MA , even when they're inappropriate to your character, as they offer new Charm and magical capabilities (as you, Murcushio, state), while the abilities your character is intended to be good at, don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T15:23:25-07:00","id":624689,"title":"","content":"Ok, I'm slightly off-topic here, but...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoEP: Sidereals, p124</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only the Maidens themselves could devise these means of influencing the Tapestry of Creation without snarling it beyond repair,and only they have the power to design new Charms that fall outsidethe scope of those listed here. <u>Over the millennia, the Maidens have devised new Charms as they became necessary</u>, creating new branches to the original trees. This happens very rarely, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not headcanon, not &quot;what if&quot;, it's right in the beginning of the charm section. The Maidens can and did create new charms. They don't do it often, but they do it.<br /> The charmset was never as hermetically &quot;no new charms, ever&quot; closed as it's often made out to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T15:35:45-07:00","id":624693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=624406#post624406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that was a 2nd edition mistake but it goes back to 1st edition too.<br /> I think the intention is that you travel off-screen but it would be amusing if having a scene of the PCs conversing among themselves or encountering something in the air caused the charm to end abruptly and as a result Sidereals with that charm having lots of pockets that are perpetually full of small rodents in case of unforseen circumstances in the air.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder what Mercury has against montages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T15:47:55-07:00","id":624696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=624256#post624256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other odd thing about Riding the Dragon is that it was created before the Primordial War, and lesser elemental dragons didn't exist until a century or something after the War ended. It's like the weirdness of the anti-undead Medicine charms, except those revealed their purpose as soon as the first Neverborn died.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were likely added by the Maidens after there was a reason to add them. Remember, the maidens can add new charms if they want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T15:56:41-07:00","id":624698,"title":"","content":"Heh, thinking about the Charms and the Sutra and the fact that it's under Journeys... Sidereal magic sees &quot;riding&quot; in terms as a metaphor for what the world does to you while getting things from place to place. The child being driven to a new home because of an opportunity in the career of their parents is a dumb animal that knows not where it is going or why, but must bear the burden of this incomprehensible thing that sits astride their back and pulls on their reigns. A Sidereal is the one who rides you; they piggyback on your destiny to get them to their literal or abstract destination. If your destiny is not fast enough, they can make you become fast. Contemplation of this reveals truths about Journeys. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T16:11:30-07:00","id":624707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=624696#post624696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were likely added by the Maidens after there was a reason to add them. Remember, the maidens can add new charms if they want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone who wishes to integrate <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-exalted-3rd-edition/posts/884408\" target=\"_blank\">some of EX3's fluff</a> into things could opt for an even simpler rationale: elementals would be far older than the Primordial War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T16:16:57-07:00","id":624708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=624252#post624252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, that runs into conflict with other Sidereal themes, one of which is their closed Charmset.<br /> <br /> With a closed Charmset, damn near every Sidereal is going to be initiated into Sorcery and learn Martial Arts, because the Sidereal Charmset is optimized fully for them in their role as Viziers to the Solars and agents of the Bureau of Destiny, and it works great for those two things but is complete shit at anything else. Astrology is more flexible but is subtle rather than direct and also limited in scope. (Let's ignore for a bit the bad mechanics behind it.)<br /> <br /> Sidereals who want to expand their skillsets flexibly and powerfully have to learn Sorcery and/or Martial Arts. That's a major theme behind them and one of the bedrocks of their design, that Sidereals are sifus and sorcerers, unable to flexibly channel their essence in the way other Exalted can but masters of the martial arts and with their fingers on the strands of fate.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the Sidereals still have much of their infrastructure in place and unlike the Dragon-Blooded don't have a societal taboo against sorcery.<br /> <br /> With all those facts in place, it is usually safe to assume any Sidereal of any age at all has at least been initiated into sorcery and knows a few spells, if for no other reason than that Spell-Shattering Palm, while pretty great, is hard to learn and not nearly as flexible as Sapphire Countermagic, and the work they do means they're going to bump up against assholes wielding the Emerald Circle an awful lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay so, I think you make a good point here. The Sidereal closed charmset forcing them to, as they gain experience and cultivate their essence, explore non-native avenues of development is something I have always liked about them (and it also naturally pushes them towards being sorcerers and sifus, as you say). I do also think that Sorcery should retain it's weird mystique, though. I remember reading Scroll of Exalts and Ayesha Ura has all of that stuff about how she sacrificed her love for the big C and her identify as a Bronze Faction member to become a Sorcerer, which is cool and compelling, but the big guy himself is just a really powerful Sorcerer, with no explanation of what he sacrificed, how he initiated, how he changed as a result. Almost like Sorcery is just some charms he learnt rather than a strange and dangerous path to esotoric power.<br /> <br /> I feel that Sorcery should always be the former, where it's a big deal, and not something suitable for all characters at all (so the question is always &quot;how did you become a Sorcerer?&quot; rather than &quot;why didn't you learn Sorcery?&quot;. Which is hard to reconcile with Elder Sidereals all pretty much running into their closed charmset wall and looking at Sorcery and thinking &quot;that'd be cool to know.&quot; Especially as Ride the Dragon is a higher essence power, so it's the kind of thing that even a Siddie previously uninterested in Sorcery learns before hitting that wall and thinking &quot;what now then?&quot;<br /> <br /> So the Charm does kind of make itself redundant in that way, you're right. I dunno. I think it would be a better Charm if you had two options, turn them into a mighty dragon who obeys your every command like a taxi-cab with a minigun on the roof (very useful!) or you can make them permanently that and also not annihilate their personality but if you do they are u<i>nder no obligation to actually do anything you say. </i>Also the Dragon would be a proper full on source of power, especially as in Ex3 the combat system probably won't be so focused on paranoia that anything which hasn't invested in it becomes a waste of time, and we know that Sorcery is being toned down when it comes to fast travel, so it'll be inherently more appealing in terms of speed as well.<br /> <br /> I think the conflict there is a bit more interesting, because the moral question is more a case of dare you let your creation act of it's own freedom, or are you simply concerned with full control over the power it brings? You could do the right thing and not annihilate their mind, but if you do, then you just created a Dragon which remembers being a mortal. Maybe that will have some nasty repercussions. But if you need the power and you don't want your conscience to be burdened...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T16:27:08-07:00","id":624713,"title":"","content":"Nobody should be treating sorcery like a standard-issue multi-tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T16:39:54-07:00","id":624719,"title":"","content":"Reading this thread and thinking about the many ways in which Sidereal charms encourage them to be jerks makes me think that Rakan Thulio's personal crusade is an in-setting catharsis/guideline for everyone that doesn't like stuff like Shun the Smiling Lady, Ride the Dragon, and general fishboning. Maybe the 3E understanding is that as a Sidereal player, sooner or later you have to come to terms with the fact that you work for the Bureau of Callous Dickery, and you need to decide whether you're okay with that or not.<br /> <br /> Earlier editions gave us plenty of example NPCs that somehow deal- Chejop, Ayesha, etc. have come to terms with working through the Bureau of Callous Dickery, and being willing to accept varying degrees of compromise regarding how much the world sucks in exchange for some scrap of stability. Alongside them, 3E gives us the PC who halfway through the campaign gives the Maidens the finger and sets off on his own, to bring true justice to the cosmos with his own two fists. The Getimians are, in part, an option for players who want to make that rebellion the whole focus of their campaign, rather than a midway point of character development.<br /> <br /> Of course, 3E may also downplay the emphasis on callousness as a component of Sidereal power.<br /> <br /> Edit: Maybe Rakan's unforgivable crime was like, punching the Loom or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","user":"GhostTurtle","date":". 08-12-2015, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T09:53:27-07:00","id":625637,"title":"","content":"I honestly think that we are going to see a massive revamp on how Siddy charms work, come 3rd Edition. They will still have a closed charm tree, because that's kinda their schtick...but there are some things about them that are getting changed. It has been explicitly said that a Sidereal is not required to branch off into Martial Arts to remain viable in high-xp combat.<br /> <br /> First off, they are no longer pariahs in Yu Shan, with everyone trying to screw them over. The devs have been pretty clear that the Siddies are well respected people doing an important job. (Possibly because most of the Siddies who were around during the Usurpation are dead now)<br /> <br /> Secondly, it's been acknowledged that the Siddy charm tree was rubbish in many places...and they have said that they would 'be shocked' if the Sidereal Charm Tree didn't see the same sort of expansion as the Solar tree has seen.<br /> <br /> As to the character concepts... John Morke says:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> there have been problems with the way Sidereals have been depicted, especially in how they operate mindlessly and without question, and especially in how the gods seethe with hatred and resentment for them. This is shit that will be corrected. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think the 2E writers made a bit of a mistake with that 'choke on a fishbone' mission thing that they dropped into the MoEP. It made it look like that's how they always operated. Because the thing is...a Sidereal's job is to make sure that Fate goes the direction it needs to go. Sure, a Chosen of Endings may have a tendency to push Fate along their chosen path by stabbing anyone who might interfere...but there are plenty of other options.<br /> <br /> Say...you need to prevent the rising of a tyrant. A child has been born who, if untampered with, will rise up to be a horrible tyrant who colludes with the Fair Folk, and leads to a vast number of deaths.<br /> A Chosen of Endings may simply make sure the child doesn't survive to adulthood.<br /> A Chosen of Journeys may instead bring about events that relocate the child and their family to somewhere where they won't have the same Fate, or give the child experiences that pushes them towards a path as a traveling merchant<br /> A Chosen of Serenity may ensure that the child has such a happy life that they grow up as a well-adjusted member of society.<br /> A Chosen of Battles may ensure that as the child grows, they are pitted in conflict with the Fair Folk so that, while they still become a powerful ruler, their blade is turned against the forces of chaos, instead of towards seizing rulership<br /> A Chosen of Secrets may tamper with the child's education and upbringing so that, while they still come into a powerful ruling position, they are instead a fair and just ruler who leads his people well.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, Sidereals have to do dirty work. Sometimes you have to excise a tumor to protect the whole. But sometimes, you get to terminate a plague instead. Sometimes you get to arrange the meeting and romance of a destined couple. Sometimes you are the traveler who stops in a tavern and encourages a young man to set out on the road to seek his fortune.Sometimes you're the old man on the mountain who advises the hero in his quest.<br /> <br /> Some days, you have to do terrible things. But you aren't blind and you aren't stupid. You can look into the future and see the results of what you are about to do the same as your superiors can. You don't have to obey without question. You can find another way. You can expose the corruption of your superiors. You've got a hard job for sure....you often have to make tougher calls than any of the other Exalted because you know more about the shape of the world than they do...but it is worth it. Some days...one must die to save a thousand. Others days...one must be protected to saved a thousand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T12:53:55-07:00","id":625762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=624689#post624689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I'm slightly off-topic here, but...<br /> Not headcanon, not &quot;what if&quot;, it's right in the beginning of the charm section. The Maidens can and did create new charms. They don't do it often, but they do it.<br /> The charmset was never as hermetically &quot;no new charms, ever&quot; closed as it's often made out to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, the charmset <i>is</i> hermetically sealed... from an <i>in-universe perspective</i>.<br /> <br /> Other Exalted who have been around for any period of time have either been taught or figured out that the &quot;natural&quot; applications of their essence that come to them relatively easily aren't the be-all and end-all of their potential. They can develop the way their essence interacts with the world and with themselves, their Charms, according to their own wishes. Some of them will do it through focused study and meditations, others through trial-and-error brute force, but they can actually forge new Charms to use in furtherance of whatever they decide their purpose as an Exalted is. They don't have carte blanche, of course, but there's a lot of flexibility.<br /> <br /> Sidereals can't do that. What they have is what they have. Sure, maybe the Maidens will show up tomorrow with a bunch of new ones. You can't count on that, and that's different from having control over your own essence. <br /> <br /> From the perspective of your average Five-Score Fellow, his charmset is hermetically sealed. That's always been part of the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T15:04:33-07:00","id":625969,"title":"","content":"Um, no, Murcushio, he can still walk right up to one of the Maidens and <i>ask for a new Charm</i>. The seal is as &quot;hermetic&quot; out-of-universe as it is in-universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-13-2015, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T15:44:32-07:00","id":626009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=625969#post625969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, no, Murcushio, he can still walk right up to one of the Maidens and <i>ask for a new Charm</i>. The seal is as &quot;hermetic&quot; out-of-universe as it is in-universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are the Maidens under any obligation to give it to him? And can they give the Charm JUST to him and not to all Sidereals? My understanding is that the Maidens handing down new Charms is a rare event that almost never happens, because the line developers want the Sidereals to have a closed Charmset and all that entails, and in fact they're to a certain degree balanced around having a closed Charmset. Am I wrong in this? Because if asking the Maidens for a new Charm has, for 5000 years, resulted in them going &quot;no,&quot; then functionally you can't get new Charms.<br /> <br /> And even if you could, you're still not in control of your own essence. No other Exalt, even the Terrestrials, has to petition their patron for control over their own essence. That's the point, is it not? That the Sidereal Charmset is closed off in all but the most extraordinary of circumstances. If the Maidens are handing you a new Charm, that's probably a momentous occasion, as opposed to a Solar developing custom Charms because the usual ways they have of channeling their essence aren't cutting it for them anymore, which probably happens all the damn time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T15:53:27-07:00","id":626014,"title":"","content":"&quot;Not in control of their Essence?&quot; Really?<br /> <br /> DBs can't develop a Charm to let them extrude their mouths on tentacles - guess they're not in control of their Essence, either. (Hell, they can't even go to their patrons and ask for them to change that!) They're limited to <i>just</i> human excellence filtered through the themes and associations of the five elements.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are limited, yes. All the Exalted are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-13-2015, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T15:56:13-07:00","id":626016,"title":"","content":"Yeah it's basically sealed for all practical intents and purposes.<br /> <br /> Sure, one of the Incarnae might choose to make the sealed set a bit more expansive, but they almost certainly won't. Remember, for many years in the First Age the Maidens received petitions from every Sidereal who cared to think on the subject to create more Shards because they were incredibly overworked and outnumbered by the other Celestials. The Maidens' response was a consistent and calm &quot;all is unfolding as we have forseen.&quot; They aren't in the habit of doing what Siddies want because they want it (unlike, say, the UCS, who seems considerably more open to being moved by the passion of his chosen).<br /> <br /> Anyway yes I agree with Isator. Sorcery shouldn't be treated as a multi-purpose toolkit. I don't think that does have to conflict with &quot;most Sidereals become Sorcerers after a a while&quot; though, it just means you need to ensure that all Sidereals are written with a more compelling view of Sorcery in mind.<br /> <br /> Although I do think that when it comes to exploring non-native sources of power, they are 1) more likely to turn to MA before Sorcery as a group, and 2) now have Evocations to look at as well. Which is cool. When they develop a SMA based around Evocations, that shit is going to be <i>unreal</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T15:58:25-07:00","id":626017,"title":"","content":"Notionally and semantically, I don't know how much it's like<br /> <br /> &quot;The Maidens have designed these Charms; they have given these Charms to their Exalted; they could've designed others, but didn't because Fate or their wisdom&quot;<br /> <br /> vs<br /> <br /> &quot;Among the Maidens, for example, the Maiden of Battles has dominion over close combat; these Sidereal Melee Charms are just all the techniques channeling her essence and Sidereal essence that there can be&quot; (no one is &quot;designing&quot; anything, it simply turns out that these are the Charms, that exist, from expressing the essence of the Maiden of Battles and the Sidereals with the certain economy of expression characteristic of the nature of Fate).<br /> <br /> I sort of have a preference for the latter, simply because it feels less like the Maidens are choosing the limits of the Chosen, limiting them from what they could be, so much as that is just a natural limit inherent to their essence. (trying not to leap into my typical spiel about how it's important for the Sidereals not to feel like stupid fools who do things for no reasons while facing arbitrary limits designed to frustrate them).<br /> <br /> Note this still actually allows for some expansion from the Maidens themselves, it's just that becomes more of &quot;She is changing her Essence and the Sidereal essence, which is a big deal for Fate, and now it can be channeled in new ways&quot; and not &quot;She made a new Charm or deigned to gift it to her Chosen&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T16:04:57-07:00","id":626023,"title":"","content":"Not that I have any great insight to offer, but something to consider. Each Ability charmset for Sidereals comes with a Sutra. The Sutra is obviously important to the charms though I'm not certain of the exact relationship. I would expect at the very least for any new charms developed for an Ability would need to be consistent with the Sutra. Adding something new could require that the Sutra be altered, which would be a very big deal and something the Maidens would be highly resistant to doing.<br /> <br /> Also Astrology Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T16:14:58-07:00","id":626030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=626016#post626016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, for many years in the First Age the Maidens received petitions from every Sidereal who cared to think on the subject to create more Shards because they were incredibly overworked and outnumbered by the other Celestials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slight tangent question here: The Sidereals have generally or always been overworked but it hasn't <b><i>always</i></b> been as bad as the Time of Tumult in every earlier period of history, right? The 5 years since the Empress vanished surely have to be on the high end of the workload scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T17:09:14-07:00","id":626068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=626014#post626014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Not in control of their Essence?&quot; Really?</div> </div> </div> </div>To an extent, yes. They can channel their essence into a set of very specifically defined Charms and that's it. Other Exalted can make their essence do other things, can stretch their bounds, but the Sidereals cannot; their only avenues for essence growth in that way come through Martial Arts and Sorcery.<br /> <br /> The key word in those three sentences was &quot;extent.&quot; The Sidereals aren't in control of their essence in the very specific sense that they can't make new Charms. That's a huge limitation! It doesn't mean they literally have zero control over how they expend their essence, but it does represent a huge loss of control over it that the other Exalted do not have.<br /> <br /> I feel like you're calling me out more on my usage of language in one sentence I was using for emphasis rather than actually responding to any of my substantive points here. Lord knows I use language badly a lot of the time, but when you focus on just that and respond to nothing else I was saying my response is sort of &quot;buh?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Slight tangent question here: The Sidereals have generally or always been overworked but it hasn't <b><i>always</i></b> been as bad as the Time of Tumult in every earlier period of history, right? The 5 years since the Empress vanished surely have to be on the high end of the workload scale. </div> </div> </div>That sounds about right, Erinys, especially since one imagines that faction politics were basically static before then and probably didn't involve a lot of fieldwork. Faction politics have to be undertaken in the Sidereals &quot;free&quot; time (since the Bureau doesn't give a shit about Bronze/Gold infighting, it cares about fulfilling its mandate) and one imagines that suddenly needing to keep a lid on the Solars/help the Solars is contributing to their massive workload.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T17:15:13-07:00","id":626076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=626030#post626030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slight tangent question here: The Sidereals have generally or always been overworked but it hasn't <b><i>always</i></b> been as bad as the Time of Tumult in every earlier period of history, right? The 5 years since the Empress vanished surely have to be on the high end of the workload scale.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I imagine their workload was pretty heavy (though not Age of Sorrows heavy) just before the Usurpation, when some (not all) Solars were ripping apart Creation for shits and giggles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T18:10:29-07:00","id":626090,"title":"","content":"Even the Age of Sorrows probably pales in comparison to the Time of Cascading Years, for any Sidereals who were trapped in Creation (alone!) then.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I imagine that during most of the First and Second Ages, it couldn't have been as bad as in the Time of Tumult.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oadenol must have had time to write his codex, for example. And Sidreals used to train all the other Celestials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-14-2015, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T16:02:25-07:00","id":627085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/622655-ex3-sidereals-charms-and-character-concepts?p=625762#post625762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, the charmset <i>is</i> hermetically sealed... from an <i>in-universe perspective</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, when people complain &quot;But we want some new Sidereal charms!&quot; other peole answer &quot;You can't have them, you can never have them, the charm set is closed, you would need to break canon to introduce them!&quot;, which was given as a reason for why there were never any new sidereal charms published...<br /> ...yeah, no. Introducing new charms does not break canon (not that &quot;canon&quot; is even a thing on the table - it's just a thing in the books, but even there, new charms are reasonable). Adding in new charms is perfectly possible. Heck, in Glories, the Maiden have a charm that allows them to give any sidereal praying to them a charm as a training effect, which is explicitaly called out to be combinable with their ability to create new charms - so, I sidereal in a bind can pray &quot;How in Malfeas am I supposed to prevent these bandits from killing these few puppies?&quot;, and the Maidens can answer by directly handing him a charm that allows him to give these puppies the fate of an huge wolf pack.<br /> <br /> They *can*.<br /> <br /> In character, learning Martial Arts, Sorcery, and Evocations still makes sense (though I suspect 3ed sids are going to have tons more charms and the question &quot;Oh, I ran out of groth space in my area of expertiese, what am I going to learn now?&quot; is not going to be nearly as common), since those aren't dependent on the Maidens - what I'm mostly arguing against is the out-of-character reasoning &quot;They can never get new charms, because the books said so&quot; - because the books <i>don't</i> say so. New charms are rare, but they are a thing.<br /> And besides, we have no time scale how rare &quot;rare&quot; is. Maybe once every hundred years, maybe once every thousand, maybe the last time was before the ursupation or even right around the primordial war, or whatever. Or &quot;rare&quot; means that most Sids shower the Maidens in charm requests regularily, and &quot;rare&quot; just means that of the thousands of requests each year, only one gets through each season.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T19:34:09-07:00","id":627180,"title":"","content":"It's also perfectly reasonable to look at their small charmset, or note specific holes in it, and say that the Maidens probably made more than that. You can retroactively declare that a charm was always there since the Primordial War, or since the First Age, or whatever, if it would make sense for the Maidens to consider it necessary.<br /> <br /> What the closed charmset does mean is that they often have to find sideways uses for charms because they don't have as many as other Exalted. It means they have only the tools that the Maidens consider necessary and can conceive of and design. Everything will fit their design methods, and Sidereals just have to learn to bend their thinking to work that way. They can't create a charm just because they want it, or because they think they need it when they really don't, or to help them accomplish some faction goal or side project or corruption that isn't part of their actual Maidens-given job. And the Maidens are fallible so their opinion about what's necessary may have mistakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-14-2015, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}